0$\n\nAsymptote slopes satisfy $Cr^2 + Br + A = 0$, with one root $20/17$. So $C(20/17)^2 + B(20/17) + A = 0$, i.e., $400C/289 + 20B/17 + A = 0$, multiply by 289: $400C + 340B + 289A = 0$.\n\nSo $289A + 340B + 400C = 0$. (Equation 5)\n\nNow I have 5 equations, 6 unknowns, but homogeneous so effectively 5 equations in 5 unknowns (up to scale). Let me solve.\n\nLet me subtract equations to eliminate F.\n\nEq1 - Eq3: $(4-1)A + (10-1)B + (25-1)C + (2-1)D + (5-1)E = 0$\n$3A + 9B + 24C + D + 4E = 0$ ... (I)\n\nEq2 - Eq3: $48A + 20B + 8C + 6D + 2E = 0$ → $24A + 10B + 4C + 3D + E = 0$ ... (II)\n\nEq4 - Eq3: $99A + 99B + 99C + 9D + 9E = 0$ → $11A + 11B + 11C + D + E = 0$ ... (III)\n\nEq5: $289A + 340B + 400C = 0$ ... (IV)\n\nFrom (III): $D + E = -11A - 11B - 11C$.\n\nFrom (I): $D + 4E = -3A - 9B - 24C$.\nSubtract: $3E = (-3A-9B-24C) - (-11A-11B-11C) = 8A + 2B - 13C$.\n$E = (8A + 2B - 13C)/3$.\n\n$D = -11A-11B-11C - E = -11A-11B-11C - (8A+2B-13C)/3$\n$= (-33A-33B-33C - 8A - 2B + 13C)/3 = (-41A - 35B - 20C)/3$.\n\nFrom (II): $3D + E = -24A - 10B - 4C$.\n$3D + E = 3 \\cdot (-41A-35B-20C)/3 + (8A+2B-13C)/3 = (-41A-35B-20C) + (8A+2B-13C)/3$\n$= [(-123A - 105B - 60C) + (8A + 2B - 13C)]/3 = (-115A - 103B - 73C)/3$.\n\nSet equal to $-24A - 10B - 4C$:\n$(-115A - 103B - 73C)/3 = -24A - 10B - 4C$\n$-115A - 103B - 73C = -72A - 30B - 12C$\n$-115A + 72A - 103B + 30B - 73C + 12C = 0$\n$-43A - 73B - 61C = 0$\n$43A + 73B + 61C = 0$ ... (V)\n\nNow (IV) and (V):\n$289A + 340B + 400C = 0$\n$43A + 73B + 61C = 0$\n\nSolve for A, B in terms of C (or find ratios).\n\nFrom (V): $43A = -73B - 61C$, $A = (-73B - 61C)/43$.\n\nSub into (IV): $289(-73B-61C)/43 + 340B + 400C = 0$.\nMultiply by 43: $289(-73B - 61C) + 340 \\cdot 43 B + 400 \\cdot 43 C = 0$.\n$289 \\cdot 73 = ?$ $289 \\times 73 = 289 \\times 70 + 289 \\times 3 = 20230 + 867 = 21097$.\n$289 \\times 61 = 289 \\times 60 + 289 = 17340 + 289 = 17629$.\n$340 \\times 43 = 14620$.\n$400 \\times 43 = 17200$.\n\n$-21097 B - 17629 C + 14620 B + 17200 C = 0$\n$(-21097 + 14620)B + (-17629 + 17200)C = 0$\n$-6477 B - 429 C = 0$\n$6477 B = -429 C$\n$B = -429 C / 6477$.\n\nSimplify: $\\gcd(429, 6477)$. $6477 / 429 = 15.09...$ $429 \\times 15 = 6435$, $6477 - 6435 = 42$. $\\gcd(429, 42)$: $429 = 42 \\times 10 + 9$, $42 = 9 \\times 4 + 6$, $9 = 6 \\times 1 + 3$, $6 = 3 \\times 2$. So $\\gcd = 3$. $429/3 = 143$, $6477/3 = 2159$.\n\n$B = -143 C / 2159$.\n\nCheck: $2159 = 143 \\times 15 + 14$? $143 \\times 15 = 2145$, $2159 - 2145 = 14$. $\\gcd(143, 14)$: $143 = 14 \\times 10 + 3$, $14 = 3 \\times 4 + 2$, $3 = 2 \\times 1 + 1$. $\\gcd = 1$. So $B = -143C/2159$.\n\nHmm, let me double check $2159$. $6477 / 3 = 2159$. Yes.\n\nNow $A = (-73B - 61C)/43 = (-73 \\cdot (-143C/2159) - 61C)/43 = (73 \\cdot 143 C/2159 - 61C)/43$.\n$73 \\times 143 = 73 \\times 140 + 73 \\times 3 = 10220 + 219 = 10439$.\n$A = (10439 C/2159 - 61C)/43 = C(10439/2159 - 61)/43 = C(10439 - 61 \\times 2159)/(2159 \\times 43)$.\n$61 \\times 2159 = 61 \\times 2000 + 61 \\times 159 = 122000 + 9699 = 131699$.\n$10439 - 131699 = -121260$.\n$A = C \\cdot (-121260)/(2159 \\times 43) = -121260 C / 92837$.\n\nHmm, this is getting messy. Let me reconsider — maybe I should just compute the slopes directly.\n\nThe slopes satisfy $Cr^2 + Br + A = 0$. One root is $r_1 = 20/17$. The other root $r_2 = A/(C r_1) = A \\cdot 17/(20 C)$... wait, product of roots $= A/C$, so $r_1 r_2 = A/C$, $r_2 = A/(C r_1) = A \\cdot 17/(20C)$.\n\nSo I need $A/C$.\n\n$A/C = -121260/92837$. Let me simplify. $\\gcd(121260, 92837)$. \n\n$121260 = 92837 \\times 1 + 28423$.\n$92837 = 28423 \\times 3 + 7568$. ($28423 \\times 3 = 85269$, $92837 - 85269 = 7568$)\n$28423 = 7568 \\times 3 + 5719$. ($7568 \\times 3 = 22704$, $28423 - 22704 = 5719$)\n$7568 = 5719 \\times 1 + 1849$.\n$5719 = 1849 \\times 3 + 172$. ($1849 \\times 3 = 5547$, $5719 - 5547 = 172$)\n$1849 = 172 \\times 10 + 129$.\n$172 = 129 \\times 1 + 43$.\n$129 = 43 \\times 3 + 0$.\n\nSo $\\gcd = 43$. $121260/43 = 2820$. $92837/43 = 2159$.\n\nSo $A/C = -2820/2159$.\n\nThen $r_2 = (A/C) \\cdot 17/20 = (-2820/2159) \\times 17/20 = -2820 \\times 17 / (2159 \\times 20)$.\n$2820/20 = 141$. So $r_2 = -141 \\times 17 / 2159 = -2397/2159$.\n\nSimplify $\\gcd(2397, 2159)$. $2397 - 2159 = 238$. $2159 = 238 \\times 9 + 17$. ($238 \\times 9 = 2142$, $2159 - 2142 = 17$). $238 = 17 \\times 14$. So $\\gcd = 17$.\n$2397/17 = 141$. $2159/17 = 127$.\n\nSo $r_2 = -141/127$.\n\nLet me verify: $r_2 = -141/127$. So $m = 141, n = 127$. $\\gcd(141, 127)$: $141 - 127 = 14$, $127 = 14 \\times 9 + 1$, $14 = 1 \\times 14$. $\\gcd = 1$. Good, relatively prime.\n\n$100m + n = 14100 + 127 = 14227$.\n\nWait, let me double-check the computation of $A/C$ more carefully, since there's a lot of arithmetic.\n\nLet me re-derive. We have:\n- $43A + 73B + 61C = 0$ ... (V)\n- $289A + 340B + 400C = 0$ ... (IV)\n\nFrom these two, solve for $A/C$ and $B/C$.\n\nFrom (V): $43A = -73B - 61C$.\nFrom (IV): $289A = -340B - 400C$.\n\nMultiply (V) by 289 and (IV) by 43:\n(V)×289: $289 \\cdot 43 A + 289 \\cdot 73 B + 289 \\cdot 61 C = 0$\n(IV)×43: $43 \\cdot 289 A + 43 \\cdot 340 B + 43 \\cdot 400 C = 0$\n\nSubtract: $(289 \\cdot 73 - 43 \\cdot 340)B + (289 \\cdot 61 - 43 \\cdot 400)C = 0$.\n$289 \\times 73 = 21097$. $43 \\times 340 = 14620$. $21097 - 14620 = 6477$.\n$289 \\times 61 = 17629$. $43 \\times 400 = 17200$. $17629 - 17200 = 429$.\n\nSo $6477 B + 429 C = 0$, $B = -429/6477 C = -143/2159 C$. ✓\n\nNow from (V): $43A = -73(-143/2159)C - 61C = (73 \\times 143/2159)C - 61C$.\n$73 \\times 143 = 10439$.\n$43A = (10439/2159 - 61)C = (10439 - 61 \\times 2159)/2159 \\cdot C$.\n$61 \\times 2159 = 131699$.\n$10439 - 131699 = -121260$.\n$43A = -121260/2159 \\cdot C$.\n$A = -121260/(2159 \\times 43) C = -121260/92837 C$.\n\n$A/C = -121260/92837$. Simplify by 43: $-2820/2159$. ✓\n\nProduct of roots $r_1 r_2 = A/C = -2820/2159$.\n$r_2 = (-2820/2159)/(20/17) = (-2820/2159)(17/20) = -2820 \\times 17/(2159 \\times 20) = -141 \\times 17/2159 = -2397/2159$.\n\n$2159 = 17 \\times 127$. $2397 = 17 \\times 141$. So $r_2 = -141/127$. ✓\n\nLet me verify $2159 = 17 \\times 127$: $17 \\times 127 = 17 \\times 100 + 17 \\times 27 = 1700 + 459 = 2159$. ✓\n$2397 = 17 \\times 141$: $17 \\times 141 = 2397$. ✓\n\nSo $r_2 = -141/127$, $m = 141, n = 127$, $100m + n = 14227$.\n\nLet me also verify the hyperbola actually passes through the points and is a hyperbola. The discriminant $B^2 - 4AC > 0$ for hyperbola. With $A = -2820, B = -143, C = 2159$ (scaling by $C/2159$... let me use $A = -2820, B = -143 \\times ... $hmm let me just use the ratios. Actually let me set $C = 2159$, then $A = -2820$, $B = -143$.\n\n$B^2 - 4AC = 143^2 - 4(-2820)(2159) = 20449 + 4 \\times 2820 \\times 2159$. $2820 \\times 2159 = 2820 \\times 2000 + 2820 \\times 159 = 5640000 + 448380 = 6088380$. $4 \\times 6088380 = 24353520$. $+ 20449 = 24373969 > 0$. Hyperbola. ✓\n\nNow let me verify the asymptote slopes: $Cr^2 + Br + A = 2159 r^2 - 143 r - 2820 = 0$.\nRoots: $r = (143 \\pm \\sqrt{143^2 + 4 \\times 2159 \\times 2820})/(2 \\times 2159)$.\n$143^2 + 4 \\times 2159 \\times 2820 = 20449 + 24353520 = 24373969$.\n$\\sqrt{24373969}$? $4937^2 = ?$ $4900^2 = 24010000$, $4937^2 = (4900+37)^2 = 24010000 + 2 \\times 4900 \\times 37 + 1369 = 24010000 + 362600 + 1369 = 24373969$. ✓ So $\\sqrt{} = 4937$.\n\n$r = (143 \\pm 4937)/4318$.\n$r_1 = (143 + 4937)/4318 = 5080/4318 = 2540/2159 = 20/17$? $2540/2159$: $2159 \\times 20/17 = 2159 \\times 20 / 17 = 127 \\times 20 = 2540$. ✓ So $r_1 = 20/17$. ✓\n$r_2 = (143 - 4937)/4318 = -4794/4318 = -2397/2159 = -141/127$. ✓\n\nGreat, everything checks out.\n\nNow let me verify the conic passes through the 4 points. With $C = 2159, A = -2820, B = -143$, I need D, E, F.\n\n$E = (8A + 2B - 13C)/3 = (8(-2820) + 2(-143) - 13(2159))/3 = (-22560 - 286 - 28067)/3 = -50913/3 = -16971$.\n\n$D = (-41A - 35B - 20C)/3 = (-41(-2820) - 35(-143) - 20(2159))/3 = (115620 + 5005 - 43180)/3 = 77445/3 = 25815$.\n\n$F$: from (III) $D + E = -11A - 11B - 11C = -11(-2820) - 11(-143) - 11(2159) = 31020 + 1573 - 23749 = 8844$.\n$D + E = 25815 - 16971 = 8844$. ✓\n$F = -A - B - C - D - E$ (from Eq3) $= 2820 + 143 - 2159 - 25815 + 16971 = (2820 + 143 + 16971) - (2159 + 25815) = 19934 - 27974 = -8040$.\n\nCheck point (2,5): $A(4) + B(10) + C(25) + D(2) + E(5) + F = -2820(4) + (-143)(10) + 2159(25) + 25815(2) + (-16971)(5) + (-8040)$\n$= -11280 - 1430 + 53975 + 51630 - 84855 - 8040$\n$= (-11280 - 1430 - 84855 - 8040) + (53975 + 51630)$\n$= -105605 + 105605 = 0$. ✓\n\nCheck (7,3): $-2820(49) + (-143)(21) + 2159(9) + 25815(7) + (-16971)(3) + (-8040)$\n$= -138180 - 3003 + 19431 + 180705 - 50913 - 8040$\n$= (-138180 - 3003 - 50913 - 8040) + (19431 + 180705)$\n$= -200136 + 200136 = 0$. ✓\n\nCheck (10,10): $-2820(100) + (-143)(100) + 2159(100) + 25815(10) + (-16971)(10) + (-8040)$\n$= -282000 - 14300 + 215900 + 258150 - 169710 - 8040$\n$= (-282000 - 14300 - 169710 - 8040) + (215900 + 258150)$\n$= -474050 + 474050 = 0$. ✓\n\nAll checks pass. The answer is $100m + n = 14100 + 127 = 14227$.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787222597}
